@* ToastRegion's Overview, written by hand after Alert's and Banner's: showing a toast, an action on
   it and toasts after a redirect (each previewed in each mode), the inbox demo, how long they stay
   and where they go, and what an interactive page changes. Accessibility and See also come from
   the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>The region goes in the layout once, and <Code>ToastService</Code> shows toasts in it from anywhere: a form post on a static page, or a C# handler on an interactive one. <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code> registers the service. A toast is for news that needs no place on the page, such as "Saved"; for a message beside what it's about, use an <Anchor Href="docs/components/alert">Alert</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Showing a toast</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Success</Code>, <Code>Info</Code>, <Code>Warning</Code> or <Code>Error</Code> on the injected <Code>ToastService</Code>, with an optional title after the message.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-show" />
<TextBlock>On a static page the toast is rendered in the response, so it needs no script; on an interactive page it's added in the browser at once. Show toasts in response to an action rather than in <Code>OnInitialized</Code>, which runs twice on a prerendered interactive page.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">An action on the toast</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use a <Code>ToastAction</Code> for a button such as Undo or View: its <Code>Href</Code> is followed on static pages, and its <Code>OnClick</Code> runs C# on interactive ones.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-undo" />
<TextBlock>A static page has no connection to run C# over, so a toast shown there needs an <Code>Href</Code>: one with only <Code>OnClick</Code> throws.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">After a redirect</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>ToastService</Code> before <Code>NavigateTo</Code> in a static post's handler: the toast follows to the next page in a short-lived cookie, so post-redirect-get works.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-redirect" />
<TextBlock>On an interactive page the toast goes to the browser at once, before <Code>NavigateTo</Code> loads the next page. When that page comes from the server (an interactive part of a static page, as in these examples, or <Code>forceLoad</Code>), the region is drawn again and the toast is lost: stay on the page, or show it from the page you land on.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The inbox below posts each Archive, redirects with the archived ids in the address, and offers Undo as a link back to the address without that conversation:</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-inbox" WidthSwitch />

<Heading Level="2">How long it stays</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Duration</Code> on the region for how long toasts stay, in milliseconds (5000; <Code>0</Code> keeps them open), or a toast's own <Code>Duration</Code> for one of them.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Durations</Code>
<TextBlock>By default an error stays until it's closed, and a toast with an action stays twice as long. With JavaScript off nothing closes by itself: every toast stays until its close button is used, or the next page loads.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Where they go</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Placement</Code> for the corner or edge toasts stack in: <Code>BottomEnd</Code> by default, or <Code>TopStart</Code>, <Code>TopCenter</Code>, <Code>TopEnd</Code>, <Code>BottomStart</Code> or <Code>BottomCenter</Code>. <Code>Variant</Code> draws them as alerts are drawn (<Code>Outline</Code> by default, a raised card).</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Its own words</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Label</Code> for the region's name ("Notifications") and <Code>DismissLabel</Code> for the close buttons' name ("Dismiss"), or set them for the whole app as in <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* MainLayout.razor, once for the app *@
        <ToastRegion />

        @* A page *@
        @inject ToastService Toasts

        <form method="post" @formname="save" @onsubmit="Save">
            <AntiforgeryToken />
            <Button Submit>Save</Button>
        </form>

        @code {
            private void Save() => Toasts.Success("Your changes are live.", "Saved");
        }
        """;

    private const string Durations = """
        @* Toasts stay 8 seconds, 16 with an action; errors stay until closed. *@
        <ToastRegion Duration="8000" />

        @* This one stays until it's closed. *@
        Toasts.Show(new ToastMessage("Export ready.", Status.Success, Duration: 0,
            Action: new("Download", Href: "/exports/42")));
        """;
}
